# Creating the network configuration the game asks for, on the emulated memory card, with
# Sony's configuration program from the disc (the game restarts the machine into it).
#
# Start from power-on with examples/online-lobby.rig's first part (or by hand) until the
# game says that no network configuration is available, then run this. The program draws
# its own text: use --video and 'shot' to look. Needs --eth-net: the program tests the
# connection (DHCP) before it lets the setting be saved.
#
#   triangle            configure (in the game's notice)
#   cross               add a setting          cross   memory card slot 1
#   right               past the introduction  cross, right   the Ethernet adaptor
#   cross, right        no PPPoE               cross, right   automatic address
#   cross, right        automatic DNS          cross   start the connection test
# then, after the test: cross (continue), right (keep the name), cross (save), cross
# (back to the menu), circle and left + cross (quit); the game starts again.
wait 30
tap triangle 4
wait 900
tap cross 4
wait 240
tap cross 4
wait 300
tap right 4
wait 200
tap cross 4
wait 200
tap right 4
wait 200
tap cross 4
wait 120
tap right 4
wait 200
tap cross 4
wait 120
tap right 4
wait 200
tap cross 4
wait 120
tap right 4
wait 200
tap cross 4
wait 600
tap cross 4
wait 300
tap right 4
wait 300
tap cross 4
wait 600
tap cross 4
wait 400
tap circle 4
wait 300
tap left 4
wait 30
tap cross 4
wait 600
